---@field onRelease fun(button: number, x: number, y: number, nPress: number)? Pointer button released.
---@field onHover fun(entered: boolean)? Pointer entered/left the widget's allocation.
---@field onMotion fun(x: number, y: number)? Pointer moved within the widget.
---@field onScroll fun(dx: number, dy: number)? Scroll wheel/touchpad input.
---@field icon string? Icon theme name, e.g. "audio-volume-high-symbolic".
---@field size number? Pixel size. Default 16.

--- A themed icon (GtkIconTheme lookup by name).
---@param props khoma.IconProps|string?
---@return khoma.Element
function Icon(props) end

---@class khoma.CanvasProps
---@field key string? Stable identity within a keyed list of siblings; required whenever siblings can reorder, be inserted, or removed.
---@field class string? Space-separated CSS class names, styled by the app's style.css (hot-reloaded).
---@field style table? Inline style table, compiled to a scoped CSS rule: {background="#222", border_radius=8, padding="4px 8px", [":hover"]={...}}. Underscored keys become dashed CSS properties; numbers become px.
---@field animate boolean|khoma.AnimateSpec? Tweens any changed numeric prop on the GTK frame clock (zero per-frame Lua). true animates every numeric prop; a table restricts to `props` and sets `duration`/`easing`.
---@field hexpand boolean? Expand horizontally to fill available space.
---@field vexpand boolean? Expand vertically to fill available space.
---@field halign "fill"|"start"|"center"|"end"? Horizontal alignment within the parent's allocation.
---@field valign "fill"|"start"|"center"|"end"? Vertical alignment within the parent's allocation.
---@field margin number? Uniform margin in pixels on all four sides.
---@field opacity number? 0–1.
---@field visible boolean? Default true.
---@field tooltip string? Tooltip text shown on hover.
---@field disabled boolean? Marks the widget insensitive (GTK's SetSensitive(false)).
---@field cursor string? GTK cursor name, e.g. "pointer", "grab".
---@field onPress fun(button: number, x: number, y: number, nPress: number)? Pointer button pressed.
---@field onRelease fun(button: number, x: number, y: number, nPress: number)? Pointer button released.
---@field onHover fun(entered: boolean)? Pointer entered/left the widget's allocation.
---@field onMotion fun(x: number, y: number)? Pointer moved within the widget.
---@field onScroll fun(dx: number, dy: number)? Scroll wheel/touchpad input.
---@field width number? 
---@field height number? 
---@field commands khoma.Canvas.Command[]? rect | circle | arc | line | polygon | text — see the type alias for each op's fields.

--- Imperative 2D drawing as pure data: Lua emits a command list, Go replays it onto cairo on redraw. An
--- unchanged `commands` table (deep-equal) redraws nothing. See khoma.Canvas.Command below for the op
--- vocabulary.
---@param props khoma.CanvasProps?
---@return khoma.Element
function Canvas(props) end

-- Modules (require("khoma.xxx")) -----------------------------------------

---@class khoma.process
---@field exec fun(cmd: string|string[], cb: (fun(out: string, code: number))?) One-shot: collect stdout, call cb(out, exitcode).
---@field spawn fun(argv: string|string[], opts: { onLine: (fun(line: string))?, onStderr: (fun(line: string))?, onExit: (fun(code: number))? }?): { stop: fun(), pid: number } Long-running: line-streamed callbacks; returns a handle.

---@class khoma.file
---@field read fun(path: string): string?, err: string?
---@field write fun(path: string, data: string): ok: boolean?, err: string?
---@field exists fun(path: string): boolean
---@field list fun(dir: string): string[]?, err: string?
---@field watch fun(path: string, cb: fun(content: string), intervalMs: number?): fun() stop Fires cb(content) whenever the file's mtime changes (and once immediately).

---@class khoma.json
---@field decode fun(str: string): any?, err: string?
---@field encode fun(value: any): string?, err: string?

---@class khoma.env
---@field get fun(name: string): string?
---@field home fun(): string
---@field config_dir fun(): string $XDG_CONFIG_HOME or ~/.config.
---@field data_dir fun(): string $XDG_DATA_HOME or ~/.local/share.
---@field cache_dir fun(): string $XDG_CACHE_HOME or ~/.cache.
---@field hostname fun(): string

---@class khoma.clipboard
---@field set fun(text: string)
---@field get fun(cb: fun(text: string?)) text is nil when the clipboard is empty/unavailable.

---@class khoma.ipc
---@field register fun(name: string, fn: fun(...: any): any) The handler's single return value round-trips to the CLI caller as JSON.

---@class khoma.notifications
---@field close fun(id: number) Dismiss, as if the user closed it.
---@field invoke_action fun(id: number, key: string) Fire an action button.

---@class khoma.media
---@field play_pause fun(busName: string)
---@field next fun(busName: string)
---@field previous fun(busName: string)
---@field stop fun(busName: string)

---@class khoma.hyprland
---@field dispatch fun(cmd: string): ok: boolean, output: string Runs a `hyprctl dispatch`-style command, e.g. dispatch("workspace 2").

---@class khoma.audio
---@field set fun(level: number) 0–1.
---@field set_muted fun(muted: boolean)

---@class khoma.brightness
---@field set fun(percent: number) 0–100.

---@class khoma.apps
---@field list fun(): khoma.App[] Refreshes and returns the cache filter()/launch() read from.
---@field filter fun(query: string): khoma.App[] Substring match against the cache from the last list() call.
---@field launch fun(id: string)

---@class khoma.session
---@field supported fun(): boolean
---@field lock fun()
---@field unlock fun()
---@field is_locked fun(): boolean
---@field on_failed fun(cb: fun()) Called when the compositor refuses a lock attempt (the session was NOT locked; the `Locked` store does not flip).

---@class khoma.auth
---@field check fun(service: string?, password: string, cb: fun(ok: boolean, reason: string?)) service defaults to "login".

